# The meadow, map 1, where the game starts: a field of light grass
# —terrain autotile 0 in its plain middle pattern— hedged by bushes, with
# trees, whose crowns are drawn above the hero and whose trunks block, and
# flowers. The signpost at (7, 10) and the board at (10, 11) are the
# hub's: each is under an event of the same name with no graphic —see
# `hub.toml`—, which is what stops the hero in front of them and answers
# A. The map's size, its events and the rest are in `Map0001.json`, which
# has to say the same 20x15.
#
# The ChipSet's own tables —which upper tile lets the hero through, which
# is drawn above them— are in `db/chipsets.json`.

# 20x15, 300 tiles per layer
# The two tile layers, in reading order: one id per tile, 20 per line.
# These are the ids the binary stores; what turns them into pictures is
# the chipset. Edited by hand, the count has to stay the same.
